{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/672926-redeeming-banes","id":672926,"title":"Redeeming Banes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-20T23:05:50-07:00","id":672926,"title":"Redeeming Banes?","content":"I know spirits are ultimately simple beings, up to a point, but is there any way to take a bane gaffling and try to rehabilitate it? I seem to recall some Weaver spirits defecting to Cockroach and even changing to appear more like roaches after a while. Could you find some little imp bane, or maybe a scryer even, and &quot;flip&quot; them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T02:56:28-07:00","id":673033,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of the Gifts and Rites that allow you to order around, befriend, etc. a spirit work on Banes as well. Recruiting one mechanically isn't necessarily all that hard. Though the social and practical side of it are.<br /> <br /> I think the problem with the presumption of the thread title, or the phrasing in the opening post, is that idea that Banes aren't inherently Wyrm creatures. Redeeming or rehabilitating a Bane implies that the Bane isn't in its natural state; and you can return it to such a state. Being a Wyrm spirit means its natural state is to be that way.<br /> <br /> The shift from being a general Weaver spirit, to part of Cockroach's brood is very small. Cockroach is a very Weaver-ish Totem as it is. You'd have to have a similar &quot;home&quot; brood for any Bane if you were going to try to shift its affiliations. It can't change it's core identity, so it will need a brood that embraces that.<br /> <br /> That all said, an Elder Theurge Gift can just magic up a bane into something not-bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T03:32:15-07:00","id":673043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cockroach is a very Weaver-ish Totem as it is. You'd have to have a similar &quot;home&quot; brood for any Bane if you were going to try to shift its affiliations. </div> </div> </div>Depending on the specific bane, Uktena or Grandfather Thunder seem appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:34:33-07:00","id":673259,"title":"","content":"You could probably redeem some other type of spirit that became wyrmtainted and a de facto bane. Heck, didn't the BSD totem Green Dragon start as wyld spirit and become a bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:14:23-07:00","id":673284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/672926-redeeming-banes?p=673259#post673259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably redeem some other type of spirit that became wyrmtainted and a de facto bane. Heck, didn't the BSD totem Green Dragon start as wyld spirit and become a bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, according to TB WH, Green Dragon was Gaian, not Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T10:40:49-07:00","id":673297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/672926-redeeming-banes?p=673033#post673033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with the presumption of the thread title, or the phrasing in the opening post, is that idea that Banes aren't inherently Wyrm creatures. Redeeming or rehabilitating a Bane implies that the Bane isn't in its natural state; and you can return it to such a state. Being a Wyrm spirit means its natural state is to be that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well according to lore, the Wyrm is not in its natural state, so its reasonable to think its choirs aren't either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T12:29:23-07:00","id":673347,"title":"","content":"I would think that if a Gaian spirit can become corrupted by the Wyrm (for instance: a Glade Child becoming a Blight Child), then &quot;corrupting&quot; a Bane from its natural state to one more Gaian in nature should not be impossible. I would think it would be rare, though. Turning a Scrag (literally, a spirit of murder) to a Gaian spirit would require changing its basic spiritual essence -- into something that is not-murder, which presumably is orders of magnitude more difficult and complicated than just corrupting some average spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:00:51-07:00","id":673360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/672926-redeeming-banes?p=673297#post673297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well according to lore, the Wyrm is not in its natural state, so its reasonable to think its choirs aren't either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the Wyrm is the <i>principle</i> of entropy itself that has become twisted, it's possible there is no natural state for a bane to return to at the present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:41:10-07:00","id":673482,"title":"","content":"Not all Banes are Wyrm spirits, though. Quite a few of them are corrupt Gaian, Wyld, Weaver and Other spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}